#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""board -- the fleet work board CLI, backed by Linear.

Same verbs, flags and text output lines as the mac-collab `board` it replaces,
plus --json, `whoami`, `claim --steal --reason` and `status duplicate --of`.
scripts/linear-board/README.md has the install steps, the frozen contract
table and every environment variable.

Usage:
  board list [--app A] [--status S,S] [--severity P0,P1] [--kind K] [--mine SEAT]
             [--label NAME ...] [--search TEXT] [--limit N] [--json]
  board show <id> [--json]
  board file --title T [--app A] [--severity P0..P4] [--desc D | --desc-file PATH|-]
             [--fix F | --fix-file PATH|-] [--label NAME ...]
             [--by SEAT] [--where LOC] [--env Mac|cloud] [--kind K] [--uid U] [--url URL]
  board claim <id> --by SEAT [--where LOC] [--env Mac|cloud] [--session ID ...]
             [--steal --reason TEXT]
  board status <id> <open|in_progress|addressed|completed|deployed|wontfix|duplicate|parked>
             [--by SEAT] [--resolution TEXT] [--of <id>] [--session ID ...]
  board comment <id> --by SEAT (--text TEXT | --text-file PATH|-) [--where LOC]
             [--env Mac|cloud] [--session ID ...]
  board label add|remove <id> NAME [--by SEAT]
  board stats
  board whoami

--desc-file, --fix-file and --text-file keep free text out of argv (and so out of
`ps` and shell history).  PATH must be a regular file you own, mode 0600 or 0400,
at most 64 KB of UTF-8;  `-` reads standard input, same cap.  --label, `label` and
`list --label` take only the flat workspace labels needs-owner, ask-capture,
fleet-report and stale-claim.  These are Linear-only (BOARD_BACKEND=mac-collab
refuses them).

Ids: a full board id (32 hex, with or without hyphens), a prefix of 8 or more
hex characters, or a Linear identifier such as AFC-123.

Identity: a Linear app that mints its own token by OAuth client credentials
(design section 2).  Each seat has its own app, named for the seat bot (CLAUDE
signs as "Claude"), when its credentials file <SEAT>.env sits beside Fleet.env;
a seat with no app yet, and every read without AGENT_SEAT, uses the shared
"Fleet" app.  Each app has its own token cache and lock.  The seat comes from
AGENT_SEAT, which the five write verbs require and the read verbs do not.  The
shared app cannot tell seats apart, so every issue and comment this CLI writes
starts with a seat tag line ([CLAUDE·6db9ee77]), with a seat app too.  A seat
app's writes are refused when Linear names another app as the viewer
(swapped credentials).  A claim is a claimed:<TAG> label on the issue;
seat:<TAG> labels only say who reported or touched it (the import put them on
reporters too), so they are never read as a claim.  Writes are off unless
LINEAR_BOARD_WRITES=1.  BOARD_BACKEND=mac-collab runs the old board CLI
instead (rollback).

Stdlib only, so cloud seats, the Grok Bot VM and BotFleet containers can run
it from any AI-Fleet-Coordinator checkout: python3 scripts/linear-board/board.
"""
